{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"This run is governed by Tego, which enforces the run's contract in the kernel. When Tego refuses an action, the system call fails with EACCES or EPERM (a refused command commonly exits with status 126), and the reason is written to \"$REASON\": a JSON file (v 1) whose top level is the latest refusal, with refusals counting every refusal of the run and recent listing up to the newest 32, each with its seq, reason, rule and a one-sentence text. The run's contract decides what is allowed, and the run cannot change it. Pending refusals are reported at session start and after tools or at turn end. Later session starts may repeat pending refusals before a tool or turn-end hook reports them. Scope: whole run, including startup and background work; tool call and session attribution unavailable.\n\nRefusals pending when this SessionStart hook read the reason file:\nTego, this run's access control, refused 3 actions:\n- Tego refused write \"/home/user/out-00.txt\": this run may not write to that path (rule fs.write).\n- Tego refused write \"/home/user/out-01.txt\": this run may not write to that path (rule fs.write).\n- Tego refused write \"/home/user/out-02.txt\": this run may not write to that path (rule fs.write).\n"}}
